<DocsLayout
  title="Modules & feature flags"
  path="/docs/system/modules-flags"
  description="The six optional modules, the Pennant feature-flag system, and institution settings — and when to use each."
>
  <p>
    KoAkademy composes optional functionality at three levels: <strong
      >modules</strong
    >
    (code-level, deployed), <strong>feature flags</strong> (runtime, per installation),
    and <strong>institution settings</strong> (runtime, per school). This page inventories
    all three and explains which mechanism to reach for.
  </p>

  <h2>Modules</h2>
  <p>
    Modules use <strong>nwidart/laravel-modules</strong> and are registered into the
    Filament admin panel through <code>coolsam/modules</code>
    (<code>ModulesPlugin</code> in <code>AdminPanelProvider</code>). Enabled
    state lives in <code>modules_statuses.json</code>; all six ship enabled.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Module</th>
        <th>Registers</th>
        <th>Purpose</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Announcement</strong></td>
        <td
          >Model + policy, Filament resource, admin &amp; student-portal
          endpoints, banner render hook</td
        >
        <td>School-wide announcements</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Cashier</strong></td>
        <td>Shield-protected Filament page, controllers, notifications</td>
        <td>Student balance lookup and payment posting for cashiers</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Inventory</strong></td>
        <td
          >Filament resources (products, categories, suppliers, borrowings,
          stock movements, amendments), ledger service</td
        >
        <td>Property and equipment management</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>LibrarySystem</strong></td>
        <td
          >Filament resources (books, authors, categories, borrow records),
          research papers</td
        >
        <td>Library operations</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>NotificationCenter</strong></td>
        <td
          >Template model + service, 12 template notification classes, bulk-send
          job, admin UI</td
        >
        <td>Template-based messaging</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>StudentMedicalRecords</strong></td>
        <td
          >Model with confidentiality flags, Filament cluster + resource, stats
          widget, policy</td
        >
        <td>Clinic visit records</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    A module can contain migrations, models, policies, Filament
    resources/pages/widgets, routes, controllers, jobs, and its own tests — the
    same conventions as <code>app/</code>. Module Filament resources appear in
    the admin panel automatically once the module is enabled.
  </p>

  <h2>Feature flags (Pennant)</h2>
  <p>
    Runtime flags use <strong>Laravel Pennant</strong> with the database store. Flags
    are <strong>class-based toggles</strong> in
    <code>app/Features/Toggles</code>, catalogued in
    <code>FeatureToggleRegistry</code> and enforced by the
    <code>EnsureFeatureEnabled</code> middleware. There are 36 toggles in three families:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong><code>faculty-*</code> (19)</strong> — dashboard, classes, grades, attendance,
      schedule, action center, at-risk alerts, assessments, inbox, office hours, requests/approvals,
      insights, resources, forms, toolkit, announcements, help, settings, developer
      mode.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong><code>student-*</code> (12)</strong> — dashboard, classes, tuition,
      schedule, announcements, settings, information updates, help, grades preview,
      attendance tracker, developer mode — plus signature-pad and avatar-upload capabilities.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Administrative/enrollment</strong> —
      <code>admin-developer-mode</code>, <code>online-college-enrollment</code>,
      <code>online-tesda-enrollment</code>, and
      <code>DynamicEnrollmentPolicies</code>. The dynamic-policy flag defaults
      to <code>false</code>: while off, future enrollments use the legacy
      runtime; after deliberate activation, future enrollments resolve published
      database-backed blueprints.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Operators manage flags from the <strong>Feature Toggles</strong> page in the admin
    workspace (daacreators/pennant-manager plus a custom plugin); portal middleware
    hides disabled areas without deleting data.
  </p>

  <h2>Institution settings</h2>
  <p>
    <code>GeneralSetting</code> (spatie/laravel-settings) holds institution-wide booleans
    distinct from Pennant flags: the student portal, online enrollment, clearances,
    signature capture, QR codes, the inventory and library modules, the support page,
    and transfer e-mails. These are edited in
    <strong>General Settings</strong> and seeded by the setup wizard's final step.
  </p>

  <h2>Which mechanism should you use?</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>If the capability…</th>
        <th>Use</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Is a whole optional domain (new models, screens, jobs)</td>
        <td>A <strong>module</strong></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Turns an existing screen/flow on or off at runtime</td>
        <td
          >A <strong>Pennant flag</strong> + <code>EnsureFeatureEnabled</code
          ></td
        >
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Is institution configuration an operator edits</td>
        <td>A <strong><code>GeneralSetting</code></strong> value</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Adding a new toggle</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Create a class in <code>app/Features/Toggles</code> with a <code
        >resolve()</code
      > method.
    </li>
    <li>
      Register it in <code>FeatureToggleRegistry</code> under the right family.
    </li>
    <li>
      Guard routes/pages with <code>EnsureFeatureEnabled</code> (backend) — not just
      conditional rendering (frontend).
    </li>
    <li>Cover enabled and disabled behavior with Pest tests.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="doc-callout doc-callout-caution">
    <p class="doc-callout-label">Resolver defaults matter</p>
    <p>
      A flag's <code>resolve()</code> decides the default for every installation.
      Hard-coded <code>false</code> (like
      <code>DynamicEnrollmentPolicies</code>) keeps a feature dark even when
      code ships — say so explicitly when you do this.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
